<title>JAPAN: Japan's Ex-Im Bank to guarantee loan to Mexico.</title>
<headline>Japan's Ex-Im Bank to guarantee loan to Mexico.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Export-Import Bank of Japan said on Friday it will guarantee a loan worth $250 million, to be provided by Japanese private banks, to Mexico's infrastructure development bank, Banco Nacional de Obras y Servicios Publicos (Banobras).</p>
<p>The Ex-Im bank is planning to sign an official protocol on Tuesday with Mexican President Ernesto Zedillo, who is scheduled to arrive in Tokyo on Monday for a state visit, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The loan is for upgrading the underground railway network in Mexico City, it said, adding that an improvement of the underground could ease traffic jams and reduce pollution.</p>
</text>
